  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Ask with education",
   "texto": [
    "To order is used **Ich möchte…** (would) or **Ich hätte gern…** (I would like to). «Ich will» sounds abrupt.",
    "What you ask goes to **acusativo**: **einen Kaffee** (masculine), **eine Cola** (feminine), **ein Wasser** (neutral).",
    "The waiter asks **Was möchten Sie?** (what do you want?) and **Sonst noch etwas?** (anything else?). When you serve, says **Bitte schön**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Pay",
   "texto": [
    "**Was macht das?** or **Was kostet das?** = what is it? The answer: **Das macht 9 Euro**. «Euro» does not change in plural.",
    "To order the account: **Die Rechnung, bitte** or **Zahlen, bitte**.",
    "With the quantities **no se pone «de»**: **eine Flasche Wasser** (a bottle of water), **eine Tasse Tee** (a cup of tea), **ein Glas Milch** (a glass of milk).",
    "**Ohne** = no. **Mit** = with."
   ]
